"""Set X labels (round 45), written by hand from the official pages in pages/ before any extractor ran on set X.

Set X is the sixth fresh test set, collected after the round-45 rules and the second-reading checker (with its quotation
check) were written: a country-search part (tests/heldout_x/collect.py: a search per country in English and the country's
languages, official-looking hosts only, links that name an award followed), a registry part (collect_registry.py: award
links on the pages of scholarship_agent/sources.json not taken by sets V and W) and a second search pass with government and
doctoral scholarship queries (collect.py --round2). Every address of an earlier set and every host labelled in sets T to W was
left out. 551 pages were fetched on 2026-10-23; 126 single-programme pages were labelled; the excluded pages carry a reason
(X below; pages not named there are lists, several programmes on one page, news, staff or research grants, forms, PDFs,
near-empty pages, or were not reviewed). Labels follow the reading of sets L to W: fee status, residence, enrolment,
membership and region or group names without a list are "not_stated" nationality; a cash award whose use is not stated is
"not_stated" funding (paid per month or year: "stipend_only", marked as a close call); a stated share, cap or fixed amount
towards tuition is "partially_funded"; two funding schemes on one page are "not_stated"; deadlines are applicant dates with a
year (a year taken from a heading or a publication date is a close call); cycle_status as of 2026-10-23. Close calls are
recorded per decision in AMB ("ambiguous_fields"); results are reported with and without them.
Run once to write labels.json; manifest.json then freezes it."""
import json
import sys
from pathlib import Path
M = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(M.parents[1]))
